% === provenance: Church2014HiddenDependencies ===
% CLAIM: Git's difficulty is not only missing knowledge: its state lives in
%   hidden dependencies---between the files on disk and the current branch,
%   between a local branch and the remote-tracking copy of the remote, and
%   between new files and the index (an unadded file is unknown to Git)---so
%   even professional engineers who can articulate the conceptual model
%   follow narrow ritual workflows out of fear; a `git status` that reports
%   "up-to-date with origin/master" can be hundreds of commits behind the
%   real remote.  (Used for: the three-places and local-vs-remote aspects,
%   and for the observation that conceptual understanding alone does not
%   give confidence.)
% FOUND-VIA: scholar search "hidden dependencies version control user
%   experience" -p openalex -p dblp (session "vt-git-measurement",
